  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Whiting Turner Contracting Company the shows $761M in federal contract obligations for FY2026 to date. Whiting Turner Contracting Company the received 58 awards so far this fiscal year, with an average award size of $13.1M and obligations up 24.6% year over year. Whiting Turner Contracting Company the has a multi-year obligation history that includes $730M in FY21, $355M in FY22, $675M in FY23, $503M in FY24, and $611M in FY25. Whiting Turner Contracting Company the concentrates obligations in the Commercial and Institutional Building Construction market, which accounts for $760M of FY2026 to date obligations. Whiting Turner Contracting Company the shows concentrated federal demand from the Department of Homeland Security at $559M and the Department of Defense at $202M, with smaller obligations to the General Services Administration, the Smithsonian Institution, the Department of Health and Human Services, and the National Gallery of Art. Current-year totals are partial (fiscal year to date) and figures are contract obligations except where noted as total contract values in largest-awards and expiring-contracts tables.",
